# Mercedes-Benz S-Class W116 four-door saloon, 1972-1980.
#
# The first car to be sold as the S-Class: 4,960 mm long, 1,870 mm wide,
# 1,430 mm high, 2,734 mm wheelbase (2,865 mm on the long-wheelbase SEL);
# 2.8, 3.5, 4.5 and 6.9 litre engines, with the 450 SE the usual British import.
# 473,035 built across the range. The class-4 benchmark of the 1970s beside the
# Silver Shadow and the BMW 7 E23.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercedes-Benz_W116
#
# Colours: Black, Astral Silver, Midnight Blue and Grey were period Mercedes
# finishes; the photographs show black, gold, red and white cars, which confirms
# that strong colours were offered alongside the greys.
#
# Weight: 12 in total (black 5, silver 3, blue 2, grey 2). Section F: the
# 1960s-70s class-4 row, per the register's note that the W116 was still to be
# verified for the UK; it is included here at a modest weight.
#
# Speed 200 km/h (450 SE); comfort 95/473 (line). Classes 3,4.
# Dates: 1972-1980 with a road tail to about 2000.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/mercedes-w116.blend. References:
# citycars/references/mercedes-w116/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

